# Running .NET tests

Always run tests against the **relevant test project** `.csproj`, never the whole solution. From the skeleton root:

- Core: `src/Ape.Core/Tests/Ape.Core.Tests.csproj`
- A module: `src/Ape.Modules/Ape.Module.<Name>/Tests/Ape.Module.<Name>.Tests.csproj`

Use quiet MSBuild/terminal logging so the output stays readable:

```bash
dotnet test \
  --tl:off \
  -clp:ErrorsOnly \
  src/Ape.Core/Tests/Ape.Core.Tests.csproj
```

- `--tl:off` — disable the terminal logger
- `-clp:ErrorsOnly` — MSBuild console logger, errors only

To run a single test or class, add `--filter`:

```bash
dotnet test \
  --tl:off \
  -clp:ErrorsOnly \
  --filter FullyQualifiedName~TypeOrMethodName \
  src/Ape.Core/Tests/Ape.Core.Tests.csproj
```

Do not add `-v detailed`, `--logger "console;verbosity=detailed"`, or other verbose flags unless the user asks.
